    "payload": {
      "content": "The paper is well-organized with a logical flow from theoretical analysis to empirical validation. However, there are weaknesses in notation and figure clarity. Specifically, the notation for the empirical Neural Tangent Kernel (NTK) is inconsistent (e.g., arguments in Eq. 3 vs. text), and the distinction between dataset-concatenated vectors and single samples is not explicitly defined before use. Figure 2 is complex, and its caption fails to sufficiently explain the 'neural updates' in the top and middle rows, lacking clear axis labels or descriptions. The transition from continuous-time dynamics to simplified representational dynamics relies on an assumption (NTK reduces to identity) that is not fully justified in the main text. Table 1 is clear and effectively summarizes empirical results.",
      "reviewer_dimension": "CLAR",
      "source": "a1183db720fe87be3b06a24097874fcd207b5eae4513e4317d94366712d7fbc2",
      "topic": "CLAR Review: Notation Consistency and Figure Clarity in SSL Mechanism Analysis"
